note('Author page 16; archive 34. Recasts (55) as (56), recalls the actions associated with beta, alpha and tilde alpha in (57), then introduces inverse variables in (58)–(59). The opening has an isolated rho before the norm product and no written =1: H supplies the expected equality, but it is not transcribed. The parenthetical alpha before (56) carries a hat; this differs from the surrounding tilde-alpha notation. The final sigma in (58) visibly has an inverse exponent, retained against H. The circled triple uses zeta prime; no separate third-power exponent is securely present on Pi. The crowded cancelled change of variables remains among the least secure passages, particularly its verb and erased first factor. These are reading observations, not a proof of the claimed equivalence (56).')
